[01:10.20]treasury [ˈtreʒəri]n. 国库，金库；宝库；库存；经费，资 金
[01:14.64]coupon [ˈkuːpɒn]n. 礼券，优惠券；配给券，票证；(债 券等的)息票 例 For that price, a vendor's coupon becomes the featured deal of the day in a certain city.
[01:28.20]prediction [prɪˈdɪkʃn]n. 预言；预报
[01:31.56]domicile [ˈdɒmɪsaɪl]n. 户籍；支付场所；指定期票的支付 场所 例 The organisation of the citizens of the state according to domicile is common to all states.
[01:45.48]contract [kənˈtrækt]v. 订立合同；收缩 [ˈkɒntrækt]n. 合同 搭 contract life 合同有效期 / contract out 外包 / futures contract 期货合同 / sign a contract with sb. 与某人签订合同
[02:00.24]immaculate [ɪˈmækjulət]a. 纯洁的；无污迹的；无过失的 例 Timing and technique for this project were immaculate.
[02:10.44]weaken [ˈwiːkən]v. 削弱；(使)变弱 例 Some people worry that modern technology might weaken China's culture of ancestor worship.
[02:22.92]pit [pɪt]vt. 使相斗；使对立；使竞争 n.〈美〉(交易 市场中特定商品的)交易场地；陷阱 例 He planned to pit one group of workers against another to depress wage growth. 搭 dig a pit for sb. 设圈套陷害某人 / pit... against... 使…与…竞争
[02:41.64]genuine [ˈdʒenjuɪn]a. 真实的，名副其实的；纯血统的； 诚实的，坦率的 例 There are genuine opportunities for business in such an environment.
[02:53.88]defer [dɪˈfɜː(r)]vt. 拖延，延期 vi. 服从；推迟，延期 例 The CEO of the company planned to defer certain interest payments until next year.
[03:06.48]profile [ˈprəʊfaɪl]n. 侧面；轮廓；简介，概况
[03:10.20]longstanding [ˌlɒŋˈstændɪŋ]a. 长期的；长期存在的 例 The business exchange marks the beginning of longstanding cooperation between these two companies.
[03:25.08]deprive [dɪˈpraɪv]vt. 夺去；使丧失 例 The bill would cost up to 30,000 jobs and deprive consumers of many family vehicles. 搭 deprive sb. of sth. 夺去某人某物
[03:39.48]game [ɡeɪm]n. 策略；把戏，花招；得胜；博弈；〈美 俚〉行业，职业 vi. 赌博 例 The employers and the unions played a cat and mouse game over the proposed pay increase. 搭 have the game in one's hands 有必胜把握 / play sb.'s game 做使某人获利的事，帮某人大忙 / play the deep game 暗中捣鬼 zero inventory 零库存
[04:04.44]subsidiary [səbˈsɪdiəri]n. 子公司；附属机构 a. 辅助的，次 要的；附设的
